# Inside a call's parentheses, line breaks are insignificant, so a
# single-expression lambda body keeps reading past one: the `+ one` on the
# next line joins the body. Subtle, since outside brackets the body would
# end at the line break.
#= {result: [2, 3], inputs: {xs: [1, 2], one: 1}}
xs @ map(fn x -> x
    + one)
